Excellent! Now I have the exact schema for /v3/schedules POST:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["zone_id", "phase", "flow_rate_lpm", "duration"],
  "properties": {
    "zone_id": {"type": "string", "example": "zone-7f3a"},
    "phase": {"type": "string", "enum": ["irrigation", "lighting", "combined"]},
    "flow_rate_lpm": {"type": "integer", "description": "Flow rate in liters/min; integer only"},
    "duration": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["value", "unit"],
      "properties": {
        "value": {"type": "integer"},
        "unit": {"type": "string", "enum": ["minutes", "hours"]}
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The user wants:
- zone_id: "zone-2c19" (South Bay B)
- phase: "lighting"
- flow_rate_lpm: 8 (integer, good)
- duration: 45 minutes → `{"value": 45, "unit": "minutes"}`

This is straightforward. The user's SDK probably was sending a wrong schema (maybe sending duration as just an integer instead of an object, or using a wrong phase name, etc.).

